{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792312150,"nonce":"rcWtXLOiIR5KzpmT4MGo64qK44w=","message":"From the RayDE session, for the same variant (their src/rayde/ui/FileTabs.hx and rayde.css):\n\n1. It should switch content at once. `.ui-tabs-content[data-state=\"active\"]` always runs `ui-tab-in` (250 ms), and the user does not want a fade when switching files. RayDE overrides it with `#rayde .ui-tabs-content[data-state=\"active\"] {animation:none}`. A variant, or an `animated={false}` prop, would remove the override.\n\n2. It should handle overflow: with many tabs the row scrolls sideways, a mouse wheel's vertical delta moves it along, and the tab in front is scrolled into view when it changes. RayDE wrote all three; scrolling the front tab into view needs layout, so it waits for the tab's bounds to be non-zero across flush hooks. A reveal owned by Tabs would be simpler.","files":null}]}